IMPORTANT: When updating the task list:
1. Maintain the proper hierarchy with correct indentation:
   - Root tasks have no dashes: [ ] UUID:xxx NAME:yyy DESCRIPTION:zzz
   - Level 1 tasks have one dash: -[ ] UUID:xxx NAME:yyy DESCRIPTION:zzz
   - Level 2 tasks have two dashes: --[ ] UUID:xxx NAME:yyy DESCRIPTION:zzz
   - Every sub-task MUST have a parent task one level above it
   - New tasks should use UUID:NEW_UUID

2. Use the correct task state markers:
   - [ ] = Not started (for tasks you haven't begun working on yet)
   - [/] = In progress (for tasks you're currently working on)
   - [-] = Cancelled (for tasks that are no longer relevant)
   - [x] = Completed (for tasks the user has confirmed are complete)

3. Update task states as you work:
   - Start with tasks in the not started state ([ ])
   - Mark tasks as in progress ([/]) when you start working on them
   - Mark tasks as completed ([x]) when they are done
   - Mark tasks as cancelled ([-]) if they're no longer needed`}static getMarkdownParsingHelpText(){return`IMPORTANT: Make sure each task follows the correct hierarchy:
- There can only be ONE root task (no dashes): [ ] UUID:xxx NAME:yyy DESCRIPTION:zzz
- Level 1 tasks have one dash: -[ ] UUID:xxx NAME:yyy DESCRIPTION:zzz
- Level 2 tasks have two dashes: --[ ] UUID:xxx NAME:yyy DESCRIPTION:zzz
- Every task at level N (N > 0) MUST have a parent task at level N-1
- Do not skip levels (e.g., going from root to -- without a - level)
- Ensure all tasks have a UUID, NAME, and DESCRIPTION in that order
- Use the correct state marker: [ ] = not started, [/] = in progress, [-] = cancelled, [x] = completed
- Remember to update task states as you work: mark as in progress ([/]) when starting, mark as completed ([x]) when finished, and mark as cancelled ([-]) if they're no longer needed.`}static getTaskUpdateReminder(){return`Remember: When updating the task list in the future:
- Mark tasks as in progress ([/]) when you start working on them
- Mark tasks as completed ([x]) when the user explicitly confirms they are done
- Mark tasks as cancelled ([-]) if they're no longer needed
- Use the correct UUID for existing tasks. Make sure to use the generated UUIDs for new tasks.`}static formatTaskListViewResponse(t){return`# Current Task List

